---
title: Search & Filters
name: Search & Filters
description: Filtering list views today, and what's planned for a richer search and faceted-filter experience.
---

## Current behavior: `?filter=`

List views support filtering a single field via a query parameter:

```
/admin/user?filter=role:admin
```

This performs an equality (or, for numeric fields, coerced-equality) match
on the given field and re-renders the list with the filter applied.

### Known limitation

Because there is currently no whitelist restricting which fields can be
filtered this way, `?filter=` can currently be pointed at any field on a
model — including ones marked `hidden`. Combined with the fact that only
`Int` values are coerced correctly today (a `Boolean`, `Float`, `BigInt`,
or `DateTime` field sent through `?filter=` can produce a server error), we
recommend not relying on `?filter=` against sensitive or non-`Int` fields
in its current form. A hardened, whitelisted design is planned — see below.

## Planned: text search and faceted filters

A more capable design is planned for a future release, replacing
`?filter=` with:

- **Free-text search** (`?q=...`) across a configurable set of `searchFields`
  per model, matched with `contains` and OR'd across fields.
- **Faceted filters** (`?f.<field>=<value>`, or `?f.<field>__<op>=<value>`
  for operators like `gte`/`lte`/`contains`), rendered as a sidebar of
  filter links for low-cardinality fields (`Boolean`, `enum`) and as a
  `<select>` beyond a configurable threshold.
- A closed, type-derived **operator whitelist** — the query string only
  ever selects from a fixed, per-type set of operators, and never
  constructs an arbitrary Prisma clause from user input.
- Sensitive and `hidden` fields are excluded from filtering entirely, the
  same way they're excluded from list views (see
  [Field Types](/docs/field-types)).
- The existing `?filter=` parameter will continue to work during a
  deprecation period once the new format ships, routed through the same,
  now-whitelisted, pipeline.

This page will be updated with concrete configuration examples once the
feature ships. Track `CHANGELOG.md` for the release that adds it.
